root = TaxonomyBrowser(
  "Haystack Component Taxonomy",
  [
    indexingPipeline,
    queryPipeline,
    documentStore,
    customComponents,
    indexingPipeline2,
    queryPipeline2,
    documentStore2,
    customComponents2,
  ],
)

indexingPipeline = TaxonomyCategory(
  "Indexing Pipeline",
  "Offline ETL Processing",
  "Folder",
  "blue",
  "An Indexing Pipeline processes raw data (PDFs, HTML, Markdown) into structured, searchable Documents. It runs offline or as a batch job, converting files, splitting text, computing embeddings, and writing to the Document Store.",
  "The indexing pipeline is strictly decoupled from the query pipeline. It runs independently and its output is the Document Store. Common components: FileConverter → TextSplitter → DocumentEmbedder → DocumentWriter.",
  "Like a library cataloging system — books are received, classified, tagged, and shelved before anyone can search for them.",
  "File conversion, text chunking, embedding computation, and document persistence.",
  [
    "PDF/HTML/Markdown conversion",
    "Text splitting and chunking",
    "Embedding computation",
    "Metadata extraction",
    "Duplicate detection",
  ],
  ["Real-time query processing", "LLM answer generation", "User-facing search"],
)

queryPipeline = TaxonomyCategory(
  "Query Pipeline",
  "Real-Time Retrieval",
  "Folder",
  "green",
  "A Query Pipeline executes in real-time to answer user queries. It embeds the query, retrieves relevant documents, optionally ranks them, and may invoke an LLM for RAG-based answering.",
  "Query pipelines are latency-sensitive. They typically chain: TextEmbedder → Retriever → Ranker → PromptBuilder → LLM. The pipeline can be simplified to just Retriever for pure search without LLM generation.",
  "Like a librarian who receives your question, finds relevant books from the catalog, and presents the most relevant pages.",
  "Query embedding, document retrieval, ranking, and LLM-powered answer generation.",
  [
    "Query embedding",
    "Semantic search",
    "Hybrid retrieval (BM25 + vectors)",
    "Document ranking",
    "RAG prompt assembly",
  ],
  ["File conversion", "Batch indexing", "Document persistence"],
)

documentStore = TaxonomyCategory(
  "Document Store",
  "Persistent Storage",
  "Folder",
  "mauve",
  "The Document Store is the central persistence layer where indexed Documents live. It is not a pipeline component but a database accessed by pipeline components. Haystack supports multiple backends with different capabilities.",
  "Choose InMemoryDocumentStore for prototyping. For production, OpenSearchDocumentStore and ElasticsearchDocumentStore offer hybrid search (BM25 + vectors + metadata filtering). Vector-only stores like Chroma and Weaviate are suitable for pure embedding search.",
  "Like the physical shelves of a library — where all the cataloged books are stored and retrieved from.",
  "Document persistence, vector indexing, keyword indexing, and metadata filtering.",
  [
    "Vector similarity search",
    "BM25 keyword search",
    "Metadata filtering",
    "Duplicate policies (OVERWRITE, SKIP, FAIL)",
    "Custom document schemas",
  ],
  ["Text conversion", "Embedding computation", "Prompt templating"],
)

customComponents = TaxonomyCategory(
  "Custom Components",
  "Extensibility Layer",
  "Folder",
  "peach",
  "Custom Components let you inject any Python logic into a Haystack pipeline. You define inputs, outputs, and the processing logic, then the framework handles serialization, type validation, and pipeline wiring.",
  "A custom component requires the @component decorator, a run() method with typed inputs, and output type declarations. Use dataclasses.replace() for document mutations and copy.deepcopy() for nested structures. Components can be packaged and shared as integrations.",
  "Like building a custom shelf unit for your library — you design it to fit your specific storage needs, then plug it into the existing cataloging system.",
  "Custom preprocessing, proprietary algorithms, external API integrations, and specialized ranking logic.",
  [
    "@component decorator pattern",
    "Typed input/output sockets",
    "Pipeline serialization compatibility",
    "Component testing",
    "Integration packaging",
  ],
  ["Built-in component replacement", "Document Store implementation", "Pipeline orchestration"],
)

